{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "שבתון שבת קודש", :translit "shabbaton shabbat kodesh", :gloss "a solemn rest, a sabbath of holiness"} {:he "ויקהל", :translit "vayakhel", :gloss "and he assembled"} {:he "קודש שבת שבתון לה'", :translit "kodesh shabbat shabbaton la'", :gloss "holiness sabbath solemn rest to the LORD"} {:he "את שבתותי תשמרו", :translit "et shabbtotai tishmeru", :gloss "My sabbaths you shall keep"} {:he "לא יצא החייט במחטו סמוך לחשיכה", :translit "lo yetzei ha-chayat be-machto samuch le-chashechah", :gloss "the tailor shall not go out with his needle near dark"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word-order comparison: שבתון precedes שבת in Exodus 16:23; reversed in Exodus 35:2."} {:kind :other, :note "Word-order comparison: שבת precedes שמירה in Leviticus 19:3; שמירה precedes שבת in Exodus 31:13."} {:kind :other, :note "Mishnah Shabbat 1:3 cited as the legal precedent forbidding deriving benefit from work performed on Shabbat."}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'to add from the profane to the holy' expresses the rabbinic principle of tosefet Shabbat, accepting the Sabbath slightly early and extending it slightly late (Rosh Ha-Shanah 9a). The Mishnah prohibits a tailor from going out with his needle close to dark on Friday (Shabbat 1:3). The Talmud extends this to prohibit bathing in a bathhouse heated on Shabbat for an Israelite's needs, as a form of forbidden benefit from Sabbath labor (Beitzah 22b; Shabbat 39a).", :sources ["Rosh Ha-Shanah 9a" "Shabbat 1:3" "Beitzah 22b" "Shabbat 39a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Word-order comparison: שבתון precedes שבת in Exodus 16:23; reversed in Exodus 35:2.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Word-order comparison: שבת precedes שמירה in Leviticus 19:3; שמירה precedes שבת in Exodus 31:13.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Mishnah Shabbat 1:3 cited as the legal precedent forbidding deriving benefit from work performed on Shabbat.", :by :selah, :ran? false}]